id: pm-puf5rq
title: "GH-1291: Windows nightly release cleanup fixture includes Node compile cache"
description: "Scheduled Nightly Validation run 35841395212 on main bd8942329b8aebbc7482ce6536135535968c0e1d failed only on Windows Node 24. The release-workspace-cleanup integration test expected its TEMP/TMP root to contain only an unrelated sentinel after installer refusal, but a Node module compile cache directory appeared there. Identify whether the directory belongs to release cleanup or test-runtime cache and preserve the meaningful owned-workspace assertion."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,gh-1291,nightly,temp-cleanup,windows
created_at: "2026-09-23T18:24:56.022Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-23T20:52:43.623Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-23T20:50:37.416Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-23T20:50:37.416Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "The Windows Node 24 nightly release cleanup test distinguishes Node process compile cache from owned release workspace residue without weakening the sentinel and refusal checks; Focused regression and exact full coverage/static gates pass, and a hosted Windows Node 24 nightly run verifies the fix before GitHub issue closure"
parent: pm-p5u6
resolution: Disabled Node compile cache only for the cleanup fixture child and made plugin launcher tests use host-native paths and npm command selection.
expected_result: Windows Node 24 nightly verifies release-owned workspace cleanup without treating Node runtime cache as residue and passes plugin launcher tests.
actual_result: "Focused cleanup 3/3 and plugin portability 11/11 passed; hosted Nightly runs 35905763390 and 35917009573 passed Windows Node 24, with both final shards under 12 minutes."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-xjy565,incident_from,"2026-09-23T18:24:56.022Z","harness:codex","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-23T18:24:56.022Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all-status PM records for GH-1291, release-workspace-cleanup, Node compile cache and Windows nightly; no item owns this exact September 23 run. Reusing open temp-footprint parent pm-p5u6 and linking the previously completed release-workspace delivery pm-xjy565. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1291 and https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/35841395212."
  "2026-09-23T18:25:29.116Z","harness:codex","Investigation: GH #1291 run 35841395212 at bd8942329b8aebbc7482ce6536135535968c0e1d has one failing test, tests/integration/release-workspace-cleanup.integration.spec.ts. The assertion expected only unrelated.txt but saw node-compile-cache under the fixture TEMP/TMP root. Node documentation states module.enableCompileCache without a directory defaults to os.tmpdir()/node-compile-cache, and NODE_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE=1 disables it. The directory is a runtime optimization, not an owned release workspace; the fixture should disable it for child processes while still refusing residual owned directories."
  "2026-09-23T18:53:39.337Z","harness:codex","Hosted Nightly Validation run 35903171778 at branch head b5cdf086 passed Ubuntu 22/24/25 and macOS 24. Windows Node 24 progressed past the original release-cleanup fixture but exposed six new plugin-test portability failures: the race assertion assumed npm rather than npm.cmd and two explicit launcher fixtures used POSIX /tmp paths. Updated tests to assert the platform-selected command and construct native absolute temporary paths. Focused local regression: 11/11 passed. Re-run hosted Windows before closing."
  "2026-09-23T19:22:51.413Z","harness:codex","Hosted evidence: Nightly Validation run 35905763390 at 544c19398 completed Windows Node 24 successfully, including the release-workspace cleanup fixture and 9,243-test platform suite. Ubuntu Node 24 was independently canceled at the serial 20-minute job limit; tracked as pm-ul9rye, and its coverage/static gates are now being separated. Linked regression tests pass 3/3 cleanup and 11/11 plugin portability."
  "2026-09-23T20:50:34.109Z","harness:codex","Final hosted proof: Nightly run 35917009573 at 0e1270bc5da2d1a890b7067c5a1e68abe48b9bb1 passed all seven jobs. Windows shards 1/2 and 2/2 passed in 10m15s and 11m58s; the earlier unsharded Windows run 35905763390 also passed the original cleanup regression. Focused cleanup and native-path/plugin tests passed locally. The fixture disables only Node compile cache in its child process; owned workspace residue and unrelated sentinel assertions remain intact."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-23T20:50:34.716Z","harness:codex","On Windows Node 24, a redirected TEMP/TMP root can receive node-compile-cache from the Node runtime. Disable that optimization in a fixture whose purpose is to enumerate release-owned cleanup residue, then keep the residue assertions unchanged. Plugin launcher tests must construct host-native absolute paths and expect the platform-selected npm command."
